response:
Oh, what an exciting choice! If I were hosting a dinner party filled with historical figures, it would be like a mini-UN, full of diverse perspectives and stories. I'd love to gather a mix of people from different times and places, here’s who might make the guest list:

1. Albert Einstein - To explore the mysteries of the universe and chat about how he thinks about problems;
2. Marie Curie - She's been a pioneer that opened new worlds in science;
3. Mahatma Gandhi - His journey in understanding peace and non-violence can inspire the world;
4. Ada Lovelace - Dive into the birth of computer science and the future of technology she envisioned;
5. Nelson Mandela - Reflecting on his life and his story of resilience and struggle;
6. Leonardo da Vinci - Imagine exploring the Renaissance and beyond;
7. Anne Frank - A young voice that captured so many hearts.

Wouldn’t it be wonderful to spend time listening to their thoughts and stories, and have some meaningful conversations with these remarkable minds?
